// {{project.name}} — a kernel starting point on QEMU's RISC-V `virt` machine.
//
// WHAT IS UNDER THIS FILE, AND WHAT IS NOT
//
// No C library, no startup object, no runtime: the manifest declines the
// target's C library, so beneath this source there is the compiler, the
// instruction set, and the board package.
//
// WHAT THE BOARD PACKAGE CONTRIBUTES, AND WHY IT IS NOT NOTHING
//
// Three things this program cannot derive and should not guess:
//
//   the memory map    where this machine begins executing (0x80000000) and
//                     where its stack can go — the board's `virt.ld`, which
//                     also exports the `__stack_top` the entry stub below uses
//   the console       `board::println` writes the machine's UART; the address
//                     is the board's to know
//   the emulator      which one boots this machine, and with which arguments
//
// The sibling template writes all three into the project. Compare them: what
// changes is not what the program does but how much of this board's datasheet
// is copied into it.
import mcpplibs.riscv_virt_rt;

extern "C" void kmain() {
    board::println("{{project.name}}: running with no C library");

    // ⚠️ NO `printf` ON THIS TIER, AND THE ABSENCE IS DELIBERATE. Formatting is
    // the C library's work; a board package that grew its own would be a small,
    // worse one. A project that wants it adds `std-freestanding` with the
    // `nolibc` feature and imports <format>.
    board::println("answer 42");

    // Ends the run on the firmware's terms rather than on the emulator's
    // timeout, which is what lets `mcpp run` report a verdict at all.
    board::poweroff();
}

// The first instruction executed. `_start` establishes a stack and enters C++;
// `__stack_top` is defined by the BOARD's linker script, not by this project.
//
// `.text.entry` is placed first by that script, because execution begins at the
// load address rather than at whichever function the linker chose to put there.
asm(".section .text.entry\n"
    ".globl _start\n"
    "_start:\n"
    "  la sp, __stack_top\n"
    "  call kmain\n"
    "1:\n"
    "  j 1b\n");
